# The lf image compiles crates/ (the repository's .dockerignore leaves it out for
# the other images); BuildKit reads this file instead of it for deploy/lf/Dockerfile.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.git
# Same trap as `.env*` below: a bare `.next` matches only the context ROOT, so a
# developer's `apps/web/.next` — build output AND a webpack cache keyed to host
# paths — was riding into the image and poisoning the build inside it.
.next
**/.next
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.vercel
**/*.log
# `.env*` alone matches only the context ROOT, so `apps/api/.env` was being
# copied into the image — a developer's local secrets baked into a layer.
.env*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
.obsidian
.claude
/tmp
target
**/target
# Not inputs to this image: (the engine ships as the committed wasm
# artifacts under packages/movement-lang/wasm), the planning folders, and the
# dev-loop's and agents' transient state. `target` and `**/target` above are
# the Rust build output, which is gigabytes on a developer's machine.
plans
.superpowers
.dev-loop
.github
HEALTH.md
**/.DS_Store
